cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GUI-Primitives: A Diagnostic Benchmark and Training-Free Interventions for Spatial-Primitive Failures in VLM-based Computer-Use Agents"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "[Author]"
    given-names: "[First Author]"
abstract: >
  GUI-Primitives is a controlled, minimal-pair benchmark over seven elementary
  spatial primitives (relative-position horizontal/vertical, containment,
  list-ordinal, alignment, proximity, occlusion). Across 19 vision-language
  models, per-primitive competence rank-orders ScreenSpot-Pro grounding
  success (Spearman rho=+0.736, p=0.015, n=10). Set-of-Mark visual prompting
  recovers 35-42 accuracy points; primitive-aware CoT and activation steering
  show no robust effect. Human verification by 5 annotators yields Fleiss
  kappa=0.94 (validity) / 0.79 (target), with a 65-point ceiling gap on the
  cleaned 185-item core.
